interp=("The dataset contains a rich dense-gas signal only in HCN and HCO+ (J=2-1,3-2,4-3) plus CS 7-6; every other catalogued line in the six tunings is weak, undetected or blended. HOC+ (2-1 and 3-2) and SO 4_5-3_4 (Band 5) are tentative detections; SO 6_5-5_4, H13CN, HC3N, CH3OH, SiS, NS etc. are limits, and H13CN 4-3 is contaminated by the CO 3-2 wing so the planned opacity test must be done as an upper limit. "
"The two nuclei and the Bridge/clump regions are separable in Xb4b, Xb4d, Xb4f and Xb47 (not in Band 5), so a nuclei-vs-disk comparison is possible at 5.7x3.5\" for HCN/HCO+ 3-2 and at 4.1x2.7\" for J=4-3; the N-S pair can only be compared within the same band/beam. "
"Raw HCN/HCO+ (3-2) peak-pixel ratios are <1 almost everywhere (0.26-0.9), highest at the northern nucleus and rising towards higher resolution there (0.61 -> 0.88 -> 1.04), lowest at the S nucleus (0.4-0.5) and in the NE/E clumps (~0.3): the ratio contrast N/S is a first hint, not a result until beams are matched (Q1).")
