res('Extended disk region definition (objective)','Pixels with S/N>5 (after subtracting the r=14-22" ring zero level, -1.26 Jy/b km/s, noise 0.59) in the Xb55 HCO+ 2-1 (9.4x6.3") moment-0 map at r>8" (beyond all compact N/S/Bridge/NE/E peaks, max 7.8"): 136 pixels, 196 arcsec^2 (7.4 kpc^2), r=8-16". Stacked: HCO+ 2-1 6.3+-0.3 Jy/b km/s (24 sigma, zero-level corrected), HCN 2-1 3.2+-0.1 (37 sigma), HCN/HCO+(2-1)=0.51+-0.02 (matched Xb55 beam). Not detected beyond 8" in Xb4f HCO+ 3-2 (0.7+-0.6), HCN 3-2, Xb47 4-3, nor CH3OH (Q J=1-3 <0.07 Jy/b km/s; 2(0)-1(-1) <0.07 in Xb4f). Beam-matched test: Xb55 HCO+ 2-1 exceeds the Xb4f HCO+ 3-2 map (convolved to 9.4x6.3" and scaled at r<6") by 3.0+-0.4 Jy/b km/s at r=10-12" (2-1 more extended than 3-2, or 3-2 missing flux: Xb4f has a -0.5 Jy/b km/s zero-level bowl) - cannot separate the two','medium','scripts/disk.py, disk2.py, disk_stack.py -> out/disk_islands.csv, out/disk_stack.csv, out/disk_mask_Xb55.npz','extended disk (r>8")','statistical + empirical null (random same-size masks at r>16"); zero-level uncertainty ~0.3 Jy/b km/s','Jy/beam km/s',[A('beam','Xb55 9.4x6.3" for 2-1; 5.7x3.5" Xb4f for 3-2: the disk/nucleus ratio of 2-1 includes beam wings of the nuclear emission (beam model in disk2.py)')])
