res('CH3OH is DETECTED (replaces "unidentified 163.54 GHz" and "CH3OH not detected"): Band 5 Q-branch 165 GHz series (-1,J)-(0,J) E, J=1,2,3 blend at 163.52-163.57 GHz sky','Xb55 peak pixel (N+S+Bridge merged, 9.4x6.3"): I=2.23+-0.08 Jy/b km/s = 1.73 K km/s (27 sigma), centre 2767-2777 km/s, FWHM ~150-160 km/s (blend of three lines 20-70 km/s apart; expected width). Same line detected at all Xb55 regions defined by the merged beam. J=4 (163.659), 5 (163.836), 6, 7, 8 NOT detected: K km/s -0.06+-0.10, -0.28+-0.06, -0.09+-0.06, -0.16+-0.07, +0.05+-0.05, i.e. <~0.3 K km/s (3 sigma incl. ~0.2 baseline systematic) vs 0.9 K km/s predicted for J=4 at 30 K LTE','high','scripts/ident.py, ch3oh.py, ch3oh_lines.py, ch3oh_matched.py -> out/ch3oh_table.csv, out/ch3oh_matched.csv','N+S+Bridge merged (Xb55)','+-0.08','Jy/beam km/s',[A('rest frequencies','165.050175, 165.061130, 165.099240 GHz (CDMS); weights nu*S*mu2*exp(-Eu/10K) inside the blend'),A('v,FWHM','common, fixed to HCO+ 2-1 of the region')])
res('CH3OH 2(0)-1(-1) E (254.0154 GHz, Eu=20 K): the 251.66 GHz feature (replaces "unidentified 251.66 GHz")','Xb4f (5.7x3.5"): S 0.72+-0.07 (10.6 sigma), Soutflow 0.65+-0.08 (8.6), Bridge 0.35+-0.08 (4.6), N 0.23+-0.07 (3.2, marginal), Eclump 0.24+-0.06 (3.9); Xb4d (0.93"): Bridge 0.172+-0.016 (10.8 sigma), Wclump 0.113+-0.020 (5.8), N -0.001+-0.027, S 0.024+-0.018 (limits <0.08, <0.05); Xb4b (0.25"): Bridge 0.033+-0.007 (4.5 sigma, marginal), N,S <0.03. CH3OH/HCO+(3-2) in Xb4d = 0.051+-0.005 (Bridge), 0.051+-0.010 (Wclump), < 0.013 (N), < 0.017 (S); the emission sits on the Bridge and W clump, not on the nuclei. Identification test: line centroid vs HCO+ velocity of the same region: CH3OH requires dv=-3.5..+10.7 km/s (Xb4f S, Bridge, SWarm; Xb4d Bridge, SWarm; errors 3-17 km/s), NS 11/2-9/2 f would need -44..-58 km/s in every region (and its e partner at 253.570 is absent) -> NS rejected; SiS (+72 km/s) rejected','high (identification) / medium (fluxes)','scripts/line251.py -> out/line251_centroids.csv; out/ch3oh_table.csv; scripts/wclump.py -> out/wclump.csv','S, Soutflow, Bridge, Wclump (Xb4f/Xb4d)','see value','Jy/beam km/s',[A('rest frequency','254.015377 GHz CDMS'),A('window','template fit, v and FWHM from HCO+ of the region; beams of spw29/20 vs spw25 differ by <=7%')])
res('Matched-beam CH3OH comparison at the Band-5 peak pixel (all data convolved to 9.36x6.28" PA -88): extended vs compact, and excitation','Q J=1-3: 1.71+-0.06 K km/s; 2(0)-1(-1) E: Xb4f 0.263+-0.028, Xb4d 0.146+-0.016 K km/s (Xb4d recovers only 55+-8% of the Xb4f flux: CH3OH is extended/resolved out at 0.9"); 5(-2,4)-4(-1,3) E (Eu 57 K): 0.035+-0.032 (Xb4f), 0.018+-0.015 (Xb4d), J=4..8 Q-branch <0.3. LTE (A, Trot) fit: Trot=9 K (1 sigma 8-9, 3 sigma 7-10 K) but chi2=53 for 6 dof: LTE is not a good description (Q J=1-3 under-predicted by 1.6x). RADEX (LAMDA e-ch3oh, n 1e2-1e8, Tkin 10-200 K, eta free) also fails (chi2min 55 for 5 dof; best Tkin=10 K, n>=1e7, N/eta degenerate). Conclusion: CH3OH rotational excitation is LOW (Trot<~15 K; Eu>45 K lines absent) or non-LTE; no useful density/column constraint; beam-averaged N_u(2_0, Eu=20 K)=1.7e12 cm-2 over 9.4x6.3" (N(E-CH3OH) of order 1e13-1e14 cm-2 for Trot~10 K, uncertain by >1 dex). Q-branch/2(0)-1(-1) ratio is the discriminator','medium','scripts/ch3oh_matched.py, ch3oh_ltefit.py, ch3oh_radex.py -> out/ch3oh_matched.csv, ch3oh_ltefit_profile.csv, ch3oh_radex_grid.csv','Band-5 beam centred on phase centre','see value','K km/s',[A('10% flux calibration','added in quadrature in the LTE fit'),A('baseline systematics','negative J=5 value (-4 sigma) shows unmodelled ripple ~0.2 K km/s')])
res('Other in-band CH3OH lines','A-type J_3-J_2 cluster (249.31-249.59 GHz sky), blended with SO 6_5-5_4 (249.489): Xb4f S 0.29+-0.08 (3.6 sigma, marginal, attribution between SO and CH3OH impossible at Trot~10 K, where the Eu 60-115 K cluster is predicted ~0); 5(-2,4)-4(-1,3) E (264.364, Eu 57 K) not detected (Xb4f S 0.055+-0.082, Xb4d N 0.064+-0.020 (3.1 sigma marginal), others <2 sigma); 6(-1,5)-5(-2,4) E (262.83) within 6 MHz of the spw18/27 edge: not usable; 9(0)-8(1) E (264.92, Eu 117 K) lies on the HCO+ wing (the 16 sigma "line" at Xb4d S is the red wing of HCO+, not CH3OH): not usable; no CH3OH line with Eu<120 K and log Aij>-5 in Band 7 spws (13CH3OH only)','medium','out/ch3oh_table.csv; out/line_table_v2.csv','N, S, Bridge, clumps','1 sigma in table','Jy/beam km/s',None)
res('Line identification re-done (ident.py): all blind detections re-assigned, 132 rows in out/blind_detections_reassigned.csv','Matching on sky frequency at the LOCAL region velocity (HCO+ Gaussian centre of the same OUS) +-max(80, FWHM/2) km/s, ALL species Eu<200 K with NO Aij cut, ranked by nu*S*mu2*exp(-Eu/30K) within the species expected in LIRGs, exotic species only as fallback. Previous failure: logAij>-3.9 cut (CH3OH logA=-4.63) and species labels with electronic-state text ("SO 3Sigma v=0") not matched. Results: 163.54 = CH3OH; 251.66-251.68 = CH3OH 2(0)-1(-1); 176.95-176.98 = SO 5(4)-4(3) (178.605); 177.33 = HOC+ 2-1 (tentative); 265.96 = HOC+ 3-2 (tentative); 249.58 (5 sigma, Xb4f Soutflow) = CH3OH A-cluster/SO; Band-7 detections at 338.906, 350.65, 352.37-352.41 GHz are spw-edge artefacts (not reproduced in the overlapping spw); 341.928 (5.6 sigma, N), 176.011 (8.3 sigma, Band 5 merged; nearest CH3SH 7(1,6)-6(1,5) E dv=-58, CH3CHO 11(2,10)-11(1,11) dv=+36 km/s) remain unassigned. Unit test scripts/test_pipeline.py recovers HCO+/HCN/CS/SO and the CH3OH lines (all pass)','high','scripts/ident.py, ident_blind.py, test_pipeline.py','all spectra','tolerance +-80-100 km/s',None,None)
res('Lines not detected at the nuclei (3-sigma integrated limits per +-200-250 km/s window, Xb4f / Xb4d / Xb4b), v2','HCN v2=1f 3-2 <0.97/<0.27/<0.12 (N); HC3N 28-27 <0.65/<0.28/<0.16; 34SO 6(6)-5(5), H2COH+, CH2NH, NH2CHO, H2C18O, CH3CN 9-8 K=0 (Band 5 <0.36), CCS 13-12, HCN v2=1f 4-3 (<1.4, Xb47), HC15N 4-3, SO 8_8-7_7, CO+ 3-2 (all in out/line_table_v2.csv); SO 6_5-5_4 (251.826): <0.67 (Xb4f), <0.23 (Xb4d), <0.10 (Xb4b) Jy/b km/s at the nuclei, but this window overlaps the CH3OH A-cluster (blend, limit applies to SO+CH3OH together)','medium','out/line_table_v2.csv','N and S','3 sigma','Jy/beam km/s',None)
res('H13CN 4-3 (345.340 GHz) upper limit with an explicit CO 3-2 wing model (Xb47 spw20 upper edge)','Template = HCN 4-3 profile of the region; CO wing fitted simultaneously (exponential, log-quadratic, log-cubic, power-law, Lorentzian; range 341.80-342.20 GHz; models with chi2/dof>1.3 rejected: Lorentzian, and the zero-CO case is excluded by chi2=695-1456 for 102 points). Accepted models: 3-sigma upper limit H13CN/HCN(4-3) < 0.09-0.11 (N), < 0.135-0.15 (S; log-quadratic/cubic only), < 0.075-0.15 (Bridge) i.e. HCN/H13CN > 9 (N), > 6.7 (S, Bridge); N best-fit alpha=0.015-0.045+-0.015 (<=3 sigma). Earlier zero-CO limits (0.15/0.45/0.24 from the half-profile) were looser but unmodelled. The limit is conditional on the wing family; with a free CO wing a real H13CN signal of this size is degenerate with the wing, so the limit is the minimum defensible; extending the fit to 342.28 GHz (CO core) gives similar numbers only for log-quadratic/cubic models','medium','scripts/h13cn.py -> out/h13cn_limits.csv, out/h13cn_fits.png','N, S, Bridge','3 sigma profile-likelihood (delta chi2=9)',None,[A('template','HCN 4-3 profile of same region, v fixed')])
res('Cross-check with the literature (Harada+2018 ApJ 855, 49, ALMA Band 3 line survey of NGC 3256; Sato+2022 A&A, APEX/NOEMA)','Agreements: CH3OH, SO, HOC+ and HCN/HCO+ detected there too; Harada+ report the largest chemical variation in CH3OH (and SiO), and CH3OH emission at the two nuclei "not dominant", more visible in tidal arms/outflow positions - consistent with our CH3OH peaking on the Bridge and W clump and being undetected at the N and S nuclei (<1.7% of HCO+) in Xb4d. HOC+ remains tentative here (3 sigma conservative) whereas Harada+ detect it at the central position (low-excitation lines). Not checked: SiO (not covered), H2CS (blended with CS 7-6 here, limit <0.34). Cross-check made from the published abstracts/summary only (tables not reproduced); status: partial','low-medium','web: iopscience.iop.org/article/10.3847/1538-4357/aaaa70 ; arxiv.org/abs/2203.05851',None,None,None,None)
res('Which lines are in matched windows/apertures for any ratio in this report','CH3OH 2(0)-1(-1)/HCO+ 3-2: same OUS (Xb4d), same pixel, spw29/spw25 beams 0.98x0.77" vs 0.93x0.74" (<=7% area difference), HCO+ +-350 km/s and CH3OH LTE template; Q-branch/2(0)-1(-1): both convolved to 9.36x6.28" (matched.py); HCN/HCO+ 2-1 in the disk: Xb55 spw16/spw18 beams 8.6x6.0 vs 8.6x5.9" (identical stack mask); HCN/HCO+ 3-2 in the Soutflow wing: Xb4d spw27/25 beams 0.93x0.74" (same pixel, same windows). The raw ratio entry of the previous turn (peak-pixel HCN/HCO+) remains not beam matched across OUS','high','see scripts named in the entries',None,None,None,None)
interp=("Line inventory (corrected): besides HCN and HCO+ (J=2-1,3-2,4-3) and CS 7-6, CH3OH is detected (Band 5 165 GHz Q-branch J=1-3 at 27 sigma; 2(0)-1(-1) E at 254.015 GHz at 10 sigma), SO 5(4)-4(3) (Band 5, 8 sigma) is detected, HOC+ is tentative; everything else is a limit, blended or an edge artefact. "
"CH3OH is cold/subthermal (Q-branch J>=4 and Eu>45 K lines absent; LTE Trot~9 K, but LTE and RADEX fits are poor) and extended: the Xb4d (0.9\") CH3OH flux is only ~55% of the 9\"-beam value, and in Xb4d it peaks on the Bridge and a W clump, not on the N and S nuclei (CH3OH/HCO+ 0.05 there vs <0.015 at the nuclei) - a shock/low-excitation tracer signature that agrees qualitatively with Harada+2018. "
"The extended disk is defined (Xb55 HCO+ 2-1 S/N>5 at r>8\", HCN/HCO+(2-1)=0.51) but is not detected in the 3-2/4-3 data with the available sensitivity/zero-level. The southern blue-shifted component 1.9\" south of S is statistically solid (7-12 sigma after null calibration, 0 null peaks above 8 sigma in 583 beams), has no red counterpart, is not a PSF-sidelobe copy of S, and has HCN/HCO+(3-2)~1.8 versus 0.4 at S; it is a separate broad component at ~2560-2650 km/s. "
"The N and S nuclei are separable in Xb4b, Xb4d, Xb4f, Xb47 (not in Band 5). The opacity test (H13CN) can only give HCN/H13CN>7-9 (conditional on the CO-wing model). Raw HCN/HCO+ (3-2) peak ratios (N 0.6-1.0, S 0.4-0.5) are preliminary and not beam matched across OUS (Q1).")
cav=cav+["CH3OH LTE/RADEX fits have chi2/dof ~9-11: the numbers Trot=9 K and n>=1e7 are formal; the robust statement is 'Q-branch J>=4 absent: low excitation'. Baseline ripple of ~0.2 K km/s is visible in Band 5 (J=5 at -4 sigma).",
"Local-velocity matching (not 2780 km/s) is essential for identifications at S (2710-2740 km/s): at vsys the 251.66 feature would favour NS; at local velocity it clearly favours CH3OH.",
"The zero level of Xb4f/Xb55 moment-0 maps at r>8\" is biased by about -0.5 / -1.3 Jy/b km/s (negative bowl, missing short spacings); disk fluxes are zero-level-corrected with the r=14-22\" ring and carry >=0.3 Jy/b km/s systematic.",
"Soutflow position error is dominated by the assumed 10% beam pointing floor (0.10\"), not by the fit (0.01-0.02\"); wing definition relative to v_S=2722; comparison with the CO outflow geometry (Sakamoto+2014, Michiyama+2018) has not been made quantitatively.",
"H13CN limit conditional on the CO-wing family; log-quadratic/cubic wings can absorb a genuine H13CN signal.",
"Literature cross-check is from abstracts/summaries (Harada+2018, Sato+2022), not their tables."]
